Unions 
• Can only access one member at a time. Union stores all 
data in same chunk of memory. 
union data{ 
int x; char y; 
}; 
union data mydata; 
mydata.y = 'a'; 
mydata.x = 1; 
printf(“%d\n”, mydata.x) // Will print out 1 
printf(“%c\n”, mydata,y) // Will print out JUNK! 
